{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b163a3ae-574a-4eb1-b747-3693a736b5a5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b284228f67289bec","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-g3nku_ju/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E001.md","content":"# AMD Instinct validation campaign — vLLM ROCm serving functional and performance parity\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: whether vLLM serving on AMD\nInstinct accelerators achieves functional and performance parity for the\nplatform's supported model set. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD\nInstinct hardware using upstream (unproductized) ROCm vLLM builds, and produces\nthe parity data plus the go/no-go scope that determines which models the\nproductized ROCm serving runtime will support. The platform currently ships\nonly CUDA runtime builds and has no first-hand ROCm parity data, so this\ncampaign is the gate for all serving productization work in this strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the campaign methodology: per-model functional pass/fail criteria and\n  performance parity measurement (relative to the existing CUDA runtime builds)\n  for every model in the supported model set.\n- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or partner-lab\n  coordination) — the access itself is externally controlled and tracked as a\n  risk; the epic's deliverable is the validated data.\n- Execute vLLM ROCm serving for each model in the supported model set on the\n  dedicated AMD Instinct hardware, covering the serving configurations the\n  platform supports for the CUDA runtime.\n- Collect functional results (correctness, failures, workarounds) and\n  performance measurements per model.\n- Produce a validation report stating, per model: functional parity outcome,\n  performance parity data, and the overall go/no-go scope for productization —\n  the explicit list of models cleared for productization.\n- Record which upstream ROCm runtime image versions were validated.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A validation report exists that covers every model in the supported model\n  set, with a per-model functional pass/fail outcome and performance\n  measurements obtained on AMD Instinct hardware.\n- The report's performance data is comparable against the CUDA baseline for\n  the same model set, so parity can be assessed per model.\n- The report states the go/no-go scope for productization as an explicit list\n  of cleared models (possibly empty, in the no-go case).\n- The report records the upstream ROCm runtime image versions and hardware\n  configuration used, so results are reproducible.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n  establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization. This\n  epic delivers that campaign and its report in full.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Hardware access (procurement or partner-lab) is unresolved and externally\n  controlled; it gates campaign execution but is not a condition the campaign's\n  deliverable produces, so it is tracked here rather than as an acceptance\n  criterion.\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities; the campaign validates the versions available at execution time.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43363,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5bada63446137aa","agent_id":"ae375e71e6ea8f29e","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"4fb24c23-5a39-45d7-a47e-6c03c0269e24","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:26:32.412Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
