{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c6cee46e-ab3b-4e22-9faa-3d2fd0532cce","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-adcf8447cb6b4880","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-g3nku_ju/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a supported, productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the\nmodels the validation campaign clears. Today the platform ships only CUDA\n(NVIDIA) builds of its serving runtimes; ROCm builds exist upstream but are not\nshipped or supported. This epic turns the validated ROCm capability into a\nproductized runtime image with its serving-runtime packaging, scoped to the\nmodel list produced by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome.\n\n## Description of Dependencies\n\nThis epic's scope is gated by the validation campaign's go/no-go result: it\nproductizes exactly the models the campaign clears. If the campaign clears only\na subset of the supported model set, the scope is rewritten to that subset; a\nfull no-go removes the productization work entirely.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build and release the vLLM ROCm runtime image from the midstream vLLM repo,\n  pinned to the upstream ROCm base image version validated by the campaign.\n- Provide the serving-runtime packaging (ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime)\n  that deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime under KServe InferenceServices, aligned\n  with how the CUDA vLLM runtime is packaged today.\n- Limit the supported/declared model scope to the models cleared by the\n  validation campaign.\n- Verify KServe InferenceService deployments using the ROCm serving runtime\n  (raw deployment mode) — KServe itself requires no code changes for ROCm\n  (passive component), so this verification is an acceptance criterion here\n  rather than separate work.\n- Declare the support status and supported model list for the productized\n  runtime.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The vLLM ROCm runtime image builds green in the component's existing build\n  pipeline and is released for the target platform version.\n- The released image is pinned to the validated upstream ROCm base image\n  version, recorded in the release metadata.\n- Serving of every model on the campaign's cleared list completes successfully\n  via a KServe InferenceService using the ROCm serving runtime in raw\n  deployment mode.\n- The supported model list and support status are declared for the productized\n  runtime.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears. This epic delivers the productized\n  runtime, its packaging, and its support declaration; the KServe verification\n  (passive-component validation, same owning team) is bundled as an acceptance\n  criterion above.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities and may not align with our release trains — a schedule risk on\n  the productization timeline, mitigated by pinning the validated image\n  version.\n- Scope is parametric on the validation campaign's cleared-model list; a\n  reduced or empty outcome rewrites or removes this epic's scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44198,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5bada63446137aa","agent_id":"ae375e71e6ea8f29e","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"15e0d99c-033d-4165-8741-06665e782f60","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:26:43.478Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
