{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ca98883a-e3df-4c71-aeb3-fe1bafc929d2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cde4496002ff9f4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-g3nku_ju/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJob workloads\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers PyTorch training support on AMD Instinct accelerators\n(ROCm) for the Training Operator: platform-supported PyTorchJobs running\nsingle- and multi-GPU training on AMD GPU nodes, using a supported PyTorch\nROCm training image. Today accelerated training in the platform is validated\non NVIDIA GPUs only; this epic extends the PyTorchJob path to ROCm.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Provide a supported PyTorch ROCm training image (single- and multi-GPU) for\n  platform training workloads, built and released alongside the platform.\n- Enable PyTorchJob workloads to target AMD GPU nodes exposed through the\n  AMD device plugin (`amd.com/gpu` resource), including the job spec and\n  scheduling aspects needed for ROCm workers.\n- Validate single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJob training runs on AMD Instinct\n  nodes, including admission through the platform's workload queueing, which\n  provides the `amd.com/gpu` quota handling configured by the Distributed\n  Workloads stack.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using the supported PyTorch ROCm training image\n  completes a training run on AMD Instinct nodes.\n- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob using the supported PyTorch ROCm training image\n  completes distributed training across multiple AMD GPUs (single node and/or\n  multi-node as supported).\n- PyTorchJob workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted through the\n  platform's workload queueing and run on AMD GPU nodes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This\n  epic delivers the PyTorchJob/ROCm training slice (job support, training\n  image, and execution validation); the quota-handling slice is delivered by\n  the Kueue-side work in the Distributed Workloads stack — the two slices are\n  separate components and run in parallel, with the end-to-end admission flow\n  integration-tested by this same owning team.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Validation requires dedicated AMD Instinct hardware; access (procurement or\n  partner-lab) is unresolved and externally controlled — an availability\n  precondition tracked here rather than as an acceptance criterion.\n- Upstream PyTorch ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n  communities and may constrain which versions can be supported per release.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45687,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5bada63446137aa","agent_id":"ae375e71e6ea8f29e","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"2c5db004-c46e-4a72-af3f-24ec93cadbb0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:27:03.236Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
