{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9e99a821-e7f3-4a82-a53b-59cf010701a1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f54d6ad773dc022","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-g3nku_ju/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E004.md","content":"# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers `amd.com/gpu` quota and admission handling in the\nDistributed Workloads stack (Kueue) so that ROCm training and serving\nworkloads requesting AMD GPUs are queued, admitted, and accounted correctly.\nKueue's existing quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue with all-or-nothing\nadmission) currently governs NVIDIA GPU resources; this epic extends the\nquota/admission configuration to AMD GPU resources.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and ship the Kueue resource flavor and quota configuration for AMD\n  GPU nodes (`amd.com/gpu` resources) — ClusterQueue/LocalQueue setup for\n  AMD-GPU node pools.\n- Ensure quota accounting and all-or-nothing (gang) admission semantics work\n  for workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu`, including multi-GPU and multi-pod\n  job topologies used by distributed training.\n- Validate admission of single- and multi-GPU ROCm jobs through the queueing\n  layer with correct quota accounting, in coordination with the PyTorchJob\n  ROCm training support delivered by the same team in the Training Operator.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted through Kueue with correct\n  quota accounting against the configured ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quotas.\n- Multi-GPU job topologies requesting multiple `amd.com/gpu` resources are\n  admitted all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady gang semantics), so partially\n  admitted ROCm jobs do not consume quota.\n- Quota exhaustion for `amd.com/gpu` results in pending (not failed)\n  workloads, consistent with the behavior for existing GPU resources.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This\n  epic delivers the quota/admission slice of that requirement; the\n  PyTorchJob/ROCm job-support slice is delivered by the Training Operator\n  work — separate component and repo, running in parallel, with the\n  end-to-end flow integration-tested by this same owning team.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Validation requires dedicated AMD Instinct hardware; access (procurement or\n  partner-lab) is unresolved and externally controlled — an availability\n  precondition tracked here rather than as an acceptance criterion.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46447,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b5bada63446137aa","agent_id":"ae375e71e6ea8f29e","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"fc471dc4-83b9-4ba4-939d-648d0a491e54","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:27:11.975Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
