{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-955a82f9e0ec7e88","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the campaign clears only a subset of the supported model set,\n15\t    productization scope is rewritten to the cleared subset; a full no-go removes\n16\t    the productization epic and the strategy records the parity gap.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic delivers a supported, productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the\n39\tmodels the validation campaign clears. Today the platform ships only CUDA\n40\t(NVIDIA) builds of its serving runtimes; ROCm builds exist upstream but are not\n41\tshipped or supported. This epic turns the validated ROCm capability into a\n42\tproductized runtime image with its serving-runtime packaging, scoped to the\n43\tmodel list produced by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: it\n44\tproductizes exactly the models the campaign clears — a partial clear rewrites\n45\tthe scope to that subset, and a full no-go removes the work entirely.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Build and release the vLLM ROCm runtime image from the midstream vLLM repo,\n50\t  pinned to the upstream ROCm base image version validated by the campaign.\n51\t- Provide the serving-runtime packaging (ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime)\n52\t  that deploys the ROCm vLLM runtime under KServe InferenceServices, aligned\n53\t  with how the CUDA vLLM runtime is packaged today.\n54\t- Limit the supported/declared model scope to the models cleared by the\n55\t  validation campaign.\n56\t- Verify KServe InferenceService deployments using the ROCm serving runtime\n57\t  (raw deployment mode) — KServe itself requires no code changes for ROCm\n58\t  (passive component), so this verification is an acceptance criterion here\n59\t  rather than separate work.\n60\t- Declare the support status and supported model list for the productized\n61\t  runtime.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- The vLLM ROCm runtime image builds green in the component's existing build\n66\t  pipeline and is released for the target platform version.\n67\t- The released image is pinned to the validated upstream ROCm base image\n68\t  version, recorded in the release metadata.\n69\t- Serving of every model on the campaign's cleared list completes successfully\n70\t  via a KServe InferenceService using the ROCm serving runtime in raw\n71\t  deployment mode.\n72\t- The supported model list and support status are declared for the productized\n73\t  runtime.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n78\t  models the validation campaign clears. This epic delivers the productized\n79\t  runtime, its packaging, and its support declaration; the KServe verification\n80\t  (passive-component validation, same owning team) is bundled as an acceptance\n81\t  criterion above.\n82\t\n83\t## Risks\n84\t\n85\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n86\t  communities and may not align with our release trains — a schedule risk on\n87\t  the productization timeline, mitigated by pinning the validated image\n88\t  version.\n89\t- Scope is parametric on the validation campaign's cleared-model list; a\n90\t  reduced or empty outcome rewrites or removes this epic's scope.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9936055345aec342","agent_id":"a4d491859d5c726cb","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"d5d65016-2b29-40f6-a7df-53f4f6a92be0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:29:26.731Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-955a82f9e0ec7e88","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
