{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e2b8019b0991c67","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling for ROCm workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers `amd.com/gpu` quota and admission handling in the\n34\tDistributed Workloads stack (Kueue) so that ROCm training and serving\n35\tworkloads requesting AMD GPUs are queued, admitted, and accounted correctly.\n36\tKueue's existing quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue with all-or-nothing\n37\tadmission) currently governs NVIDIA GPU resources; this epic extends the\n38\tquota/admission configuration to AMD GPU resources.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define and ship the Kueue resource flavor and quota configuration for AMD\n43\t  GPU nodes (`amd.com/gpu` resources) — ClusterQueue/LocalQueue setup for\n44\t  AMD-GPU node pools.\n45\t- Ensure quota accounting and all-or-nothing (gang) admission semantics work\n46\t  for workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu`, including multi-GPU and multi-pod\n47\t  job topologies used by distributed training.\n48\t- Validate admission of single- and multi-GPU ROCm jobs through the queueing\n49\t  layer with correct quota accounting, in coordination with the PyTorchJob\n50\t  ROCm training support delivered by the same team in the Training Operator.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted through Kueue with correct\n55\t  quota accounting against the configured ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quotas.\n56\t- Multi-GPU job topologies requesting multiple `amd.com/gpu` resources are\n57\t  admitted all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady gang semantics), so partially\n58\t  admitted ROCm jobs do not consume quota.\n59\t- Quota exhaustion for `amd.com/gpu` results in pending (not failed)\n60\t  workloads, consistent with the behavior for existing GPU resources.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n65\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This\n66\t  epic delivers the quota/admission slice of that requirement; the\n67\t  PyTorchJob/ROCm job-support slice is delivered by the Training Operator\n68\t  work — separate component and repo, running in parallel, with the\n69\t  end-to-end flow integration-tested by this same owning team.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks\n72\t\n73\t- Validation requires dedicated AMD Instinct hardware; access (procurement or\n74\t  partner-lab) is unresolved and externally controlled — an availability\n75\t  precondition tracked here rather than as an acceptance criterion.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9936055345aec342","agent_id":"a4d491859d5c726cb","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"9487aa27-fb2f-426c-9043-5f3b42e1d9ee","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:29:30.030Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e2b8019b0991c67","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
