ilure_impact` for that same parametric dependence.\n101\tE005 should either (a) set `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001` with a\n102\t`gate_failure_impact` (e.g., action `rewrite`: partial clear documents the\n103\tcleared subset; full no-go rewrites the docs scope to record the parity gap\n104\tand drop the supported-runtime content), or (b) drop the direct E001→E005\n105\tedge and rely on the transitive E001→E002→E005 path plus E002's existing\n106\tgate. Everything else in this criterion is correct: E001 is a genuine\n107\tInvestigation (its outcome changes E002's scope and existence), E002's\n108\t`gate_failure_impact` has both `action` and `fallback_approach` populated,\n109\tits `gated_by` target is in its direct dependencies, and all Implementation\n110\tepics produce concrete artifacts.\n111\t\n112\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n113\tType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001 carries\n114\t`investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric); E002-E005 carry `ai_signals`\n115\t(9-signal rubric); no epic mixes them. Frontmatter values match the\n116\tai-signals rationale files. Architecture-claims calibration verified against\n117\t`.context`: E002's `architecture_claims: 1` cites\n118\t`rhoai-3.0/serving-runtimes.md` (\"only CUDA (NVIDIA) builds are currently\n119\tproductized — ROCm and Gaudi builds exist upstream but are not shipped or\n120\tsupported\") — confirmed present; E003's and E004's citations\n121\t(training-operator.md: PyTorchJob primary, Kueue admission, NVIDIA GPU\n122\tnodes; distributed-workloads.md: ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model,\n123\twaitForPodsReady gang admission) — confirmed present. E005's\n124\t`architecture_claims: 0` is accurate: Documentation has no\n125\tarchitecture-context file, and the epic's content derives from the strategy's\n126\town deliverables. E001's `human_judgment_required: -1` is borderline but\n127\tjustified (procurement/partner-lab access is an unresolved external-party\n128\tdecision on the campaign's periphery).\n129\t\n130\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n131\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the HLR text. Rule-mandated ACs are\n132\tpresent: E005 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review AC; E002 has the\n133\tbuild-pipeline-green and pinned-image ACs; no epic is a replacement requiring\n134\trollback/feature-flag ACs (E002 is additive). The hardware-access\n135\tavailability precondition is correctly filed as a Risk on E001/E003/E004 and\n136\ta Health Warning rather than an AC — the ACs sit on the deliverables. No\n137\tdraft-ID references in epic bodies (references use full epic IDs in\n138\tfrontmatter only). One minor: E003's third AC (\"PyTorchJob workloads\n139\trequesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted through the platform's workload\n140\tqueueing\") overlaps E004's first AC, contradicting the decomposition's stated\n141\tper-slice AC division (quota/admission ACs on the Kueue epic) — it should be\n142\tframed explicitly as the shared end-to-end integration checkpoint or moved\n143\tto E004.\n144\t\n145\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n146\tAll strategy scope is covered: the campaign (HLR-1), productized runtime with\n147\tsupport declaration (HLR-2), both slices of training support (HLR-3), and\n148\tdocumentation (HLR-4). Both strategy open questions are carried forward, not\n149\tdropped: hardware access appears as risks on E001/E003/E004 plus a Health\n150\tWarning, and upstream ROCm cadence is handled as a pinned-image AC, a risk on\n151\tE002, and a Health Warning. Out-of-scope items (Gaudi, GPU partitioning) are\n152\trespected. KServe as an affected component is accounted for via the passive\n153\tcomponent AC on E002, with a Health Warning prescribing a new epic if\n154\timplementation disproves the assumption. Missing strategy sections (Impacted\n155\tTeams, Dependencies, formal ACs, NFRs) are explicitly flagged in Health\n156\tWarnings with the derivation of owner teams documented. No conditional\n157\tbranches are used, and none are