ing runtime.\n53\t- **Serving on ROCm**: using the productized ROCm serving runtime under KServe\n54\t  InferenceServices.\n55\t- **Training on ROCm**: running single- and multi-GPU PyTorch training jobs\n56\t  on AMD GPUs, admitted through the platform's workload queueing with\n57\t  `amd.com/gpu` quota handling.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Published documentation topics state the supported AMD hardware, the driver\n62\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list, matching the validation\n63\t  campaign results and the productized runtime's declared support scope.\n64\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented serving runtime\n65\t  and training support (reviewed by the owning engineering teams) and any\n66\t  discrepancies found in review are resolved.\n67\t- The documented model list matches the productized runtime's supported model\n68\t  list exactly — no undocumented supported models and no documented\n69\t  unsupported models.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver\n74\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list. This epic delivers that\n75\t  documentation in full; it also covers the training-support usage that the\n76\t  same strategy delivers.\n77\t\n78\t## Notes\n79\t\n80\t- Epic priority is P1, derived from the strategy's overall priority\n81\t  (Major) per the docs-authoring priority exception, not from the HLR's P2\n82\t  label.\n83\t- The docs owner team is assumed (the strategy provides no Impacted Teams\n84\t  table); confirm before submission.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c0f391946e68ced","agent_id":"a50f7e6f100bd15f3","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"9c6e6526-33a9-459b-9410-9f65012f592f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:32:36.854Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92147a54d3cf9704","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"gene