{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83855aaf5482153e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct validation campaign — vLLM ROCm serving functional and performance\n4\t  parity\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n6\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n7\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 0\n13\t  source_accessibility: 0\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -3\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# AMD Instinct validation campaign — vLLM ROCm serving functional and performance parity\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: whether vLLM serving on AMD\n31\tInstinct accelerators achieves functional and performance parity for the\n32\tplatform's supported model set. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD\n33\tInstinct hardware using upstream (unproductized) ROCm vLLM builds, and produces\n34\tthe parity data plus the go/no-go scope that determines which models the\n35\tproductized ROCm serving runtime will support. The platform currently ships\n36\tonly CUDA runtime builds and has no first-hand ROCm parity data, so this\n37\tcampaign is the gate for all serving productization work in this strategy.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Define the campaign methodology: per-model functional pass/fail criteria and\n42\t  performance parity measurement (relative to the existing CUDA runtime builds)\n43\t  for every model in the supported model set.\n44\t- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or partner-lab\n45\t  coordination) — the access itself is externally controlled and tracked as a\n46\t  risk; the epic's deliverable is the validated data.\n47\t- Execute vLLM ROCm serving for each model in the supported model set on the\n48\t  dedicated AMD Instinct hardware, covering the serving configurations the\n49\t  platform supports for the CUDA runtime.\n50\t- Collect functional results (correctness, failures, workarounds) and\n51\t  performance measurements per model.\n52\t- Produce a validation report stating, per model: functional parity outcome,\n53\t  performance parity data, and the overall go/no-go scope for productization —\n54\t  the explicit list of models cleared for productization.\n55\t- Record which upstream ROCm runtime image versions were validated.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A validation report exists that covers every model in the supported model\n60\t  set, with a per-model functional pass/fail outcome and performance\n61\t  measurements obtained on AMD Instinct hardware.\n62\t- The report's performance data is comparable against the CUDA baseline for\n63\t  the same model set, so parity can be assessed per model.\n64\t- The report states the go/no-go scope for productization as an explicit list\n65\t  of cleared models (possibly empty, in the no-go case).\n66\t- The report records the upstream ROCm runtime image versions and hardware\n67\t  configuration used, so results are reproducible.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n72\t  establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n73\t  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization. This\n74\t  epic delivers that campaign and its report in full.\n75\t\n76\t## Risks\n77\t\n78\t- Hardware access (procurement or partner-lab) is unresolved and externally\n79\t  controlled; it gates campaign execution but is not a condition the campaign's\n80\t  deliverable produces, so it is tracked here rather than as an acceptance\n81\t  criterion.\n82\t- Upstream ROCm image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n83\t  communities; the campaign validates the versions available at execution time.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8344a3e9309bc020","agent_id":"a8f683bbbe8fefecb","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"455c8a09-32b4-416c-9c0f-fe96fbe72fab","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:33:46.593Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83855aaf5482153e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
