{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6bdcf893578ff88","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJob workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support for single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJob workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers PyTorch training support on AMD Instinct accelerators\n34\t(ROCm) for the Training Operator: platform-supported PyTorchJobs running\n35\tsingle- and multi-GPU training on AMD GPU nodes, using a supported PyTorch\n36\tROCm training image. Today accelerated training in the platform is validated\n37\ton NVIDIA GPUs only; this epic extends the PyTorchJob path to ROCm.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Provide a supported PyTorch ROCm training image (single- and multi-GPU) for\n42\t  platform training workloads, built and released alongside the platform.\n43\t- Enable PyTorchJob workloads to target AMD GPU nodes exposed through the\n44\t  AMD device plugin (`amd.com/gpu` resource), including the job spec and\n45\t  scheduling aspects needed for ROCm workers.\n46\t- Validate single-GPU and multi-GPU PyTorchJob training runs on AMD Instinct\n47\t  nodes, including admission through the platform's workload queueing, which\n48\t  provides the `amd.com/gpu` quota handling configured by the Distributed\n49\t  Workloads stack.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob using the supported PyTorch ROCm training image\n54\t  completes a training run on AMD Instinct nodes.\n55\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob using the supported PyTorch ROCm training image\n56\t  completes distributed training across multiple AMD GPUs (single node and/or\n57\t  multi-node as supported).\n58\t- Shared end-to-end integration checkpoint (with the quota/admission slice\n59\t  delivered by the same team in the Distributed Workloads stack, which owns the\n60\t  quota/admission acceptance criteria): PyTorchJob workloads requesting\n61\t  `amd.com/gpu` are admitted through the platform's workload queueing and run\n62\t  on AMD GPU nodes.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n67\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This\n68\t  epic delivers the PyTorchJob/ROCm training slice (job support, training\n69\t  image, and execution validation); the quota-handling slice is delivered by\n70\t  the Kueue-side work in the Distributed Workloads stack — the two slices are\n71\t  separate components and run in parallel, with the end-to-end admission flow\n72\t  integration-tested by this same owning team.\n73\t\n74\t## Risks\n75\t\n76\t- Validation requires dedicated AMD Instinct hardware; access (procurement or\n77\t  partner-lab) is unresolved and externally controlled — an availability\n78\t  precondition tracked here rather than as an acceptance criterion.\n79\t- Upstream PyTorch ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n80\t  communities and may constrain which versions can be supported per release.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8344a3e9309bc020","agent_id":"a8f683bbbe8fefecb","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"ffc2287a-0d47-46d7-af65-81f53c32c75b","time