{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8cb72af23448e4d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Document AMD GPU (ROCm) supported hardware, drivers, and validated models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Docs\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n15\tai_signals:\n16\t  change_specificity: 1\n17\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n18\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n19\t  existing_foundation: 1\n20\t  open_questions: 0\n21\t  external_dependency: 0\n22\t  human_process_gates: -1\n23\t  repo_access: 1\n24\t  architecture_claims: 0\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 3\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n31\tgate_failure_impact:\n32\t  action: rewrite\n33\t  fallback_approach: 'The campaign''s go/no-go outcome determines the validated model\n34\t    list that is this epic''s core content: a partial clear rewrites the docs scope\n35\t    to document the cleared subset, and a full no-go rewrites the docs scope to record\n36\t    the ROCm parity gap and drop the supported-runtime and validated-model content\n37\t    (the supported-hardware and driver-prerequisite topics remain).'\n38\t---\n39\t# Document AMD GPU (ROCm) supported hardware, drivers, and validated models\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tThis epic delivers the user-facing documentation for AMD GPU (ROCm)\n44\tenablement: what AMD hardware is supported, which driver prerequisites must be\n45\tinstalled, and which models are validated for the ROCm serving runtime. It is\n46\tauthored after the implementation work so the content describes what was\n47\tactually built and validated.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\tContent outline (to be authored through the Red Hat docs content process):\n52\t\n53\t- **Supported AMD hardware**: the supported AMD Instinct accelerators and node\n54\t  requirements for serving and training.\n55\t- **Driver prerequisites**: the ROCm driver stack and device plugin\n56\t  prerequisites (`amd.com/gpu` resource exposure) for AMD GPU nodes.\n57\t- **Validated model list**: the models cleared by the validation campaign and\n58\t  supported by the productized vLLM ROCm serving runtime.\n59\t- **Serving on ROCm**: using the productized ROCm serving runtime under KServe\n60\t  InferenceServices.\n61\t- **Training on ROCm**: running single- and multi-GPU PyTorch training jobs\n62\t  on AMD GPUs, admitted through the platform's workload queueing with\n63\t  `amd.com/gpu` quota handling.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- Published documentation topics state the supported AMD hardware, the driver\n68\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list, matching the validation\n69\t  campaign results and the productized runtime's declared support scope.\n70\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented serving runtime\n71\t  and training support (reviewed by the owning engineering teams) and any\n72\t  discrepancies found in review are resolved.\n73\t- The documented model list matches the productized runtime's supported model\n74\t  list exactly — no undocumented supported models and no documented\n75\t  unsupported models.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver\n80\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list. This epic delivers that\n81\t  documentation in full; it also covers the training-support usage that the\n82\t  same strategy delivers.\n83\t\n84\t## Notes\n85\t\n86\t- Epic priority is P1, derived from the strategy's overall priority\n87\t  (Major) per the docs-authoring priority exception, not from the HLR's P2\n88\t  label.\n89\t- The docs owner team is assumed (the strategy provides no Impacted Teams\n90\t  table); confirm before submission.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8344a3e9309bc020","agent_id":"a8f683bbbe8fefecb","session_id":"83c98df4-c9fc-48fe-b897-027eac3b0312","uuid":"b223d067-fb87-4888-892e-cc54fcfd3455","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:33:50.626Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8cb72af23448e4d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
